Package: helm
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: package manager for Kubernetes
 Helm installs, upgrades and removes applications on a Kubernetes cluster
 as versioned charts: templated bundles of manifests with their default
 values, which a release tracks through upgrades and rollbacks.
 .
 No Ubuntu or Debian archive carries helm, and the vendor apt repository
 on baltocdn.com serves a certificate chain apt cannot verify, so this
 package builds it. debian/rules clones the release tag that
 debian/changelog names, checks the commit against
 debian/upstream-commit, bumps the two modules whose released versions
 carry advisories, and builds a static binary with a pinned Go toolchain.
 The upstream release binary is not repacked: it carries whatever
 toolchain and module set upstream happened to build with, and those
 accumulate advisories that only a rebuild clears.
